hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1733","**\nNarrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Kurayb: Narrated to us Ḥusayn—meaning ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī—who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd narrated to us, on the authority of Abū al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī, on the authority of Aws ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me:\n\n\Indeed"," among the best of your days is the day of Jumuʿah. On it Adam was created"," on it he was taken"," on it the Trumpet will be blown"," and on it the stupor will strike. So increase your prayers upon me on it"," for your prayers are presented to me.\""\n\nThey said: \""And how will our prayers be presented to you when you have decomposed?\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah"," the Exalted and Majestic"," has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the Prophets.\"""""
"1734","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi', who said: Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, with this chain of narration similar to it, and he said: \They mean: 'You have indeed become old.'\"""""
